# Minecraft Version(s): 26.3
## Changes:
- Added Moonweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while under the open night sky in the Overworld
- Added Sunweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while under the open daytime sky in the Overworld
- Added Rainweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while rain falls on you
- Added Emberweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while in the Nether
- Added Voidweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while in the End
- Added Tideweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while your head is underwater
- All weaves are incompatible with each other, Mending, Handyman and Sacrifice
- Added Harpoon (Fishing Rods, I-III): reeled-in mobs get yanked towards you
- Added Impale Rush (Spears, I-III): charged spear hits pin the target in place (incompatible with Lunge)
- Added Updraft (Elytras, Treasure, I-III): gliding over lava, magma or fire lifts you up
- Added Curse of Corrosion (Any Damageable): slowly drains durability in rain or underwater (incompatible with all repair enchantments)
- Added Meteor (Maces, Treasure): smash attacks after falling 8 blocks set the area on fire (incompatible with Boltbringer)
- Added Jousting (Spears, I-III): deals extra damage while riding a mount
- Added Dismount (Spears): charged spear hits knock riders off their mounts
- Added Yoink (Fishing Rods, I-III): reeling in a hooked mob steals its held item
- Added Scholar of Fishing (Fishing Rods, I-III): increases the experience you get from fishing

## Fixes:
- Daytime detection predicate for Day Protection